{
 "_doc": "Per-room sound design. `assets` are short real recordings (Freesound CC0) fetched and verified by tools/audio/items.py into public/audio/items/<asset>.mp3, with the same search/classify rules as beds.json; add `pick` to pin a reviewed Freesound id. `rooms` maps a room key to its sounds: a level id ('2'), a world-challenge scene ('25:markbook') or a School Visit context ('85:kg'). `signature` layers play over the room's bed while the player is in it: `every: [min, max]` seconds between sporadic one-shots, or `loop: true` for a quiet loop; `gain` is relative to the room bed. `spots` give each evidence hotspot (by id) the one-shot it plays when tapped. Calm register: soft, short, no laughter tracks, no intelligible words.",
